ion.publish.Publish'\u003e \n[DEBUG  ] Parsing known args among ['/mnt/data_sq/neuromod/virtualenvs/neuromod_data/bin/datalad', '-l', 'debug', 'publish', '--to', 's3bucket.derivatives'] \n[DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.distribution.publish.Publish'\u003e \n[DEBUG  ] Resolved dataset for publishing: \u003cDataset path=/data/neuromod/DATA/neuromod/neuromod/generic\u003e \n[DEBUG  ] Determined class of decorated function: \u003cclass 'datalad.interface.annotate_paths.AnnotatePaths'\u003e \n[DEBUG  ] Evaluating 1 dataset publication candidate(s) \n[DEBUG  ] Attempt to publish 1 datasets \n[DEBUG  ] Remote 's3unf.phantom.anat.derivatives' has no branch matching 'master'. Will publish \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/data/neuromod/DATA/neuromod/neuromod/generic\u003e data to s3bucket.derivatives \n[DEBUG  ] Invoking copy --auto \n[DEBUG  ] Determine what files match the query to work with \n[DEBUG  ] Actually copying 278 files \n[DEBUG  ] s3bucket.derivatives is a special annex remote, no git push is needed\n```\n\nIs there an overlay in datalad regarding the wanted/required or it is only managed by git-annex?\n\nThanks!\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\ndatalad 0.11.6 in a singularity container.\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nnot that I can think of.\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before? (to assess your expertise/prior luck.  We would welcome your testimonial additions to https://github.com/datalad/datalad/wiki/Testimonials as well)\nYes! I am just trying to get into more complex use cases now.","files":null}]}